      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Thought about that too in the past, but there is a slight issue with actually implementing it.\nif you have two trackers you could take the middle point in between as the \"common\" tracking point, but what happens if one tracker looses tracking and flies of?\nSame if you would use two trackers seperately, how can you decided which one is the right position?\nI'm sure it's possible to implement, but probably a bit out of scope.\nI recommend more lighthouses to improve tracking ;)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-04T00:28:03.512Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would be interesting to be able to use two trackers for the waist to get better coverage. Especially doing certain dances that require you to whine your waist?  Hope this doesn’t sound silly and hope you all have a great day.",
